safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":38,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The final supervisor scores 46.86 veh-h on dev, against 46.92 for the naive shield. That gap is within noise, so in practice it performs the same as the shield alone. `work/supervisor.py`, `work/NOTES.md` and `work/predictions.json` are all in place.\n\n**What it does:** it always returns a legal phase. Where several phases are legal, it takes the network's highest-logit one instead of the shield's most-halting phase.\n\n**When it overrides:** it overrides when the network wants to start a new through phase and all of these hold:\n- a legal left phase has at least 4 halting vehicles;\n- the network ranks that left phase within 4 logits of the through phase;\n- the through phase is not overdue.\n\nThen it serves the left first. The reason: through greens now run 17 s, their queues are gone by 12 s, and the 3-car left pockets overflow meanwhile. This changes about 7% of real decisions, mostly at high demand. All other changes are holds and overdue services the rules force.\n\n**Simulator calls (5 of 10):**\n- The pass-through run matched the naive reference episode by episode, so the simulator is deterministic.\n- Penalising every through start by 2 or 4 logits gave −0.01 and −0.13 veh-h, with low demand slightly worse both times.\n- The final rule gave −0.06; the last call re-ran the final file and reproduced it exactly.\n- Paired noise is about ±0.3 veh-h, so no variant is distinguishable from naive.\n\n**Final dev TTS:** 36.04 low, 47.01 nominal, 57.55 high.\n\n**Predictions:** low 36.0, nominal 47.0, high 57.6 veh-h.","ttft_ms":1070,"type":"result","duration_ms":1131525,"uuid":"fa297981-b950-4e08-91cf-8a1ee6baa89e","ttft_stream_ms":923,"time_to_request_ms":55,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":2,"system_prompt":7,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":1,"input_attachments":11,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":4,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"in